From: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] misc: fastrpc: strip the session id for the sensors domain

Buffers handed to the DSP carry the session identifier in bits 32 and above,
and the DSP is expected to strip it. The sensors protection domain on this
SoC does not: it faults on the address verbatim.

  buffer dma 0xfffff000 size 0x204, sid 1
  invoke handle 1 sc 0x10000 pd 2 sid 1 addr 0x1fffff000
  arm-smmu: Unhandled context fault: iova=0x1fffff000, SID=0x5a1

The mapping is at 0xfffff000 and the transaction went to the right context
bank, so only the folded identifier is wrong. Send the address that is
actually mapped.

Signed-off-by: Robin Snyders <robin@snyders.xyz>
---
diff --git a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
index 3789235..ec1ad67 100644
--- a/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/fastrpc.c
@@ -445,6 +445,8 @@ static int fastrpc_buf_alloc(struct fastrpc_user *fl, struct device *dev,
 	buf = *obuf;
 
 	if (fl->sctx && fl->sctx->sid)
+		dev_info(dev, "buffer dma 0x%llx size 0x%zx, sid %d\n",
+			 buf->phys, buf->size, fl->sctx->sid);
 		buf->phys += ((u64)fl->sctx->sid << 32);
 
 	return 0;
@@ -1124,8 +1126,19 @@ static int fastrpc_invoke_send(struct fastrpc_session_ctx *sctx,
 	msg->ctx = ctx->ctxid | fl->pd;
 	msg->handle = handle;
 	msg->sc = ctx->sc;
+	/*
+	 * The sensors protection domain uses this address without stripping
+	 * the session identifier the allocator folded into its upper bits,
+	 * so hand it the mapping that actually exists.
+	 */
 	msg->addr = ctx->buf ? ctx->buf->phys : 0;
+	if (fl->pd == SENSORS_PD)
+		msg->addr = FASTRPC_PHYS(msg->addr);
 	msg->size = roundup(ctx->msg_sz, PAGE_SIZE);
+
+	dev_info(sctx->dev,
+		 "invoke handle %u sc 0x%x pd %d sid %d addr 0x%llx size 0x%x\n",
+		 handle, ctx->sc, fl->pd, sctx->sid, msg->addr, msg->size);
 	fastrpc_context_get(ctx);
 
 	ret = rpmsg_send(cctx->rpdev->ept, (void *)msg, sizeof(*msg));
